WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:04.470
Thallium, because it is heavier, has two different
so-called

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:09.890
oxidation states. It can react with one atom
of chlorine per

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:14.130
thallium, or say three, and the different
chemistry between

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:19.070
thallium-one and thallium-three. Thallium
salts are very

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.699
poisonous, and there was quite a notorious
case some years

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:30.810
ago when a technician at some company, who
turned out to

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:35.460
be mad, was discovered to have been poisoning
many of his

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:42.130
colleagues with thallium and so, but it is
not a widely used

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:47.940
element, apart from a few materials that are
used. There is a

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.180
rather nice red material that is made of thallium,
which has

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.559
the rather unromantic name of KRS-5, this
is mixed bromide

00:00:56.559 --> 00:01:00.510
and iodine with thallium which is used as
windows for many

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:04.089
infrared experiments. But because thallium
is so poisonous,

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:06.050
one has to be quite careful about handling.

